  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $S:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${S}^{\u2032}.$ Therefore, ${S}^{\u2032}(15,-1).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
